  "summary": "Helm Files.Lines can fail chart rendering when a chart file is empty",
  "details": "Helm contains a denial of service vulnerability in the Files.Lines template helper in pkg/engine/files.go. When a chart template calls Files.Lines on an existing empty file, the helper indexes an empty string while checking for a trailing newline. This can cause a recovered panic and render failure in template, install, upgrade, lint, and SDK Engine.Render operations.\n\nThe affected Go modules are helm.sh/helm/v3 from 3.13.0-rc.1 before 3.21.4, and helm.sh/helm/v4 from 4.0.0-alpha.1 before 4.3.0-rc.1. The stable releases containing the fix are Helm 3.21.4 and 4.3.0. Helm 4.2.4 still contains the vulnerable implementation. The fix is also present in the 4.3.0-rc.1 prerelease.",
  "severity": [
    {
      "type": "CVSS_V4",
      "score": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N"
    }
  ],
